{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "anchor": "jobs",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Jobs"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "jobs",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Jobs are used to track progress of long running tasks. A good example for a long running task is cloning of drives and servers. Depending on the current cloud resource usage and the users preferences ( Creating Drives in a Different Availability Group (Create/Clone Avoid) ), a drive clone operation can take a while."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "jobs",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Drive cloning"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "jobs",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Server cloning"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "how-it-works",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "How it works"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "drive-cloning",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Drive cloning"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "drive-cloning",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "After successfully starting a cloning operation via the API, you will receive the definition of the newly created drive. All drives have a jobs field, containing references to the all the long running tasks executed on them. The destination, since it is a newly created drive, references only 1 job - the currently running one. The source might contain more jobs, depending on how many times it was cloned. History of completed jobs is kept for 3 days. Older jobs are discarded."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "drive-cloning",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Example clone request:"
    },
